  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Vermont totaled $336M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense led buying with $203M in obligations. Procurement activity included 3,913 awards and an average award size of $86K. Obligations fell 61.7% year over year. Historical annual obligations show FY21 $394M, FY22 $506M, FY23 $424M, FY24 $920M, FY25 $877M, and FY26 $336M. Semiconductor and Related Device Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $78.1M. Engineering Services accounts for $54.4M and Other Computer Related Services accounts for $39.3M. Top vendors include GLOBALFOUNDRIES U.S. 2 LLC at $78.1M and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $47.4M. These figures are contract obligations and FY2026 totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the FY2026 federal contracting totals in Vermont?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $203M, making defense buying the dominant factor in the state total. Semiconductor and Related Device Manufacturing obligations of $78.1M and Engineering Services obligations of $54.4M concentrated spending in a few high-value areas. Overall obligations fell 61.7% year over year, while award count totaled 3,913 and the average award size was $86K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are procurement opportunities concentrated by agency and industry?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense, Department of Veterans Affairs at $53.2M, and Department of Homeland Security at $36.7M are the top buying agencies. Semiconductor and Related Device Manufacturing at $78.1M, Engineering Services at $54.4M, and Other Computer Related Services at $39.3M are the largest industries by obligations. GLOBALFOUNDRIES U.S. 2 LLC at $78.1M and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $47.4M are the largest vendors receiving those obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Vermont?",
      "a": "Vermont received $336M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 3,913 awards with an average award size of $86K. Obligations fell 61.7% year over year, and prior annual totals include FY21 $394M, FY22 $506M, FY23 $424M, FY24 $920M, and FY25 $877M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Vermont?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $203M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $53.2M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $36.7M. Other active buyers include the Department of Labor at $12.4M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $11.2M."
    },
